# Compiled PTX kernels — regenerated at build time from the .cu files
# next to this patch. ~10MB of arch-specific binary-ish content that
# bloats git history without adding source-of-truth value.
#
# The kernels are produced by build.rs (which auto-invokes nvcc when
# .cu sources are newer than .ptx targets and nvcc + cl.exe are on
# PATH). Until build.rs handles the auto-compile, the one-shot manual
# build is:
#
#   PTX_DIR=patches/candle-kernels-0.9.2/src/ptx
#   SRC_DIR=patches/candle-kernels-0.9.2/src
#   for k in affine binary cast conv fill indexing quantized sort ternary unary; do
#       nvcc -ptx -arch=sm_80 -O3 --use_fast_math "$SRC_DIR/$k.cu" -o "$PTX_DIR/$k.ptx" -I"$SRC_DIR"
#   done
#   nvcc -ptx -arch=sm_80 -O3 --use_fast_math -std=c++17 -Xcompiler /Zc:preprocessor \
#       "$SRC_DIR/reduce.cu" -o "$PTX_DIR/reduce.ptx" -I"$SRC_DIR"
#
# Documented in build-environment.mdc; tracked under the "ship a CI
# step that produces PTX as a release artifact" follow-up so end users
# don't need nvcc + cl.exe on their build host.
src/ptx/*.ptx
